      </ul>

      <h2>3. Account Registration &amp; API Keys</h2>
      <p>To access the Hosted Services or obtain routing credentials, you must create an account and generate an API key or routing access token (RAT). You are responsible for safeguarding your credentials, configuring proper key rotation, and all activities that occur under your account.</p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>Your use of the Hosted Services must comply with our <a href="/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a>. You agree not to transmit malware, conduct denial-of-service attacks, attempt unauthorized access to infrastructure, or circumvent billing meters or rate limits.</p>

      <h2>5. Fees, Subscriptions &amp; Metering</h2>
      <p>Access to the Hosted Services is billed according to the usage rate card on our <a href="/pricing/">Pricing page</a>, measured asynchronously at our edge:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Reach:</strong> Backbone delivery to offline recipients past included monthly allowances.</li>
        <li><strong>Telemetry:</strong> Device event processing and OTLP translation past included monthly allowances.</li>
        <li><strong>Secondary Dimensions:</strong> Internet egress and long-term mailbox storage past included allowances.</li>
        <li><strong>Direct &amp; P2P:</strong> Pure peer-to-peer and local bearer traffic never incurs Hosted Service fees.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>All fees are exclusive of taxes, which will be billed where applicable. Invoices are charged automatically via your payment method on file. Unpaid balances may result in account suspension.</p>

      <h2>6. Fail-Open Architecture &amp; Suspension</h2>
      <p>Hop is designed to be fail-open. If your account hits a spending cap, fails payment, or is suspended for billing:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The managed backbone halts acceptance of new bundles from your account.</li>
        <li>Bundles already accepted keep being carried under standard at-least-once lifetime rules.</li>
        <li>Direct peer-to-peer and local mesh connections continue operating uninterrupted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We reserve the right to immediately terminate access or revoke access keys for material breaches of our Acceptable Use Policy.</p>

      <h2>7. Privacy &amp; Data Protection</h2>
      <p>Message payloads are end-to-end encrypted before leaving your devices; our relays process ciphertext and cannot inspect payload contents. Our collection and handling of account metadata and billing usage are governed by our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and, where applicable, our <a href="/dpa/">Data Processing Addendum</a>.</p>

